@* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Reports/Assets/Header.aspx (+ .aspx.cs) -> Components/Pages/Reports/Assets/Header.razor
   (checklist task 92).

   The legacy page was a STANDALONE document (its own <!DOCTYPE>/<html>/<head>/<body>, no master
   page) whose only content was an asp:PlaceHolder filled in Page_Load with

       using (ReportHeader header = new ReportHeader())
       {
           this.Placeholder1.Controls.Add(header);
       }

   CONSUMER CALL-SITE CONVERSION. ReportHeader is now the Blazor component
   MixERP.Net.WebControls.ReportEngine/ReportHeader.razor, so "new + Controls.Add" becomes the
   <ReportHeader /> element below. Its Path parameter is deliberately left unset: the original
   never assigned Path either, so the component falls back to the same default report-header
   template it always used.

   The document chrome is owned by App.razor now, so this page carries no <html>/<head>/<body>.
   <title>MixERP WebReport</title> survives as <PageTitle>. @layout BlankLayout is the migrated
   form of "no master page" (Specialist 7's note: BlankLayout is the layout for the standalone
   WebForms documents; it also supplies the master-page javascript globals that the always-loaded
   master-page bundle reads).
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *@
@page "/Reports/Assets/Header"
@layout BlankLayout
@inherits MixERPWebpage
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.ReportEngine

<PageTitle>MixERP WebReport</PageTitle>

<ReportHeader />
